     sections: [
       { h2: 'Best Free Golf App: The Grint', affiliateKey: 'the-grint', badge: 'BEST FREE', body: "Official USGA handicap tracking, GPS yardages for 40,000+ courses, scoring, and a social feed — all free. No trial period, no feature gates, no ads interrupting your round. The free tier gives you everything a casual golfer needs: distances to the green, a scorecard, and a real USGA handicap index.\n\nThe premium tier ($8/month) adds strokes gained analysis and detailed round-by-round stats. It is good data, but most golfers under 20 rounds per year will not use it enough to justify the cost. The free version alone makes The Grint the first app every golfer should install.\n\nThe one limitation: GPS accuracy depends on your phone. On an iPhone 13 or newer, yardages are within 2-3 yards of a laser rangefinder. Older phones can drift 5-8 yards. The Grint cannot match a dedicated GPS watch for speed — you are still pulling out your phone. But at zero cost, it is the baseline every other app has to beat.",
