       { h2: 'Strokes-Gained — The Real Value', body: "Monthly reports revealed something surprising: we were not losing strokes putting or driving. We were hemorrhaging 3.4 strokes per round on approaches from 125-175 yards. Our 6-8 iron distances were 7-10 yards shorter than believed, causing systematic short-side misses.\n\nThe fix was simple: club up in that range. Two months later, approach strokes-gained improved by 1.8 strokes/round. Combined with AI suggestions, total handicap improvement: 2.1 strokes over 4 months. Measurable, data-driven, directly attributable to Arccos." },
-      { h2: 'Is $99/Year Justified?', body: "Year 1: $179 + $99 = $278 ($13.90/round at 20 rounds). Year 2: $99 ($4.95/round). Year 3: $99 ($4.95/round). Three-year total: $476 for 60 rounds = $7.93/round.\n\nShot Scope V5: $249 one-time, 60 rounds = $4.15/round. Cheaper. But no AI caddie — just data. If data alone is enough, Shot Scope wins on value. If you want AI recommendations that improve scoring, Arccos is the only option.\n\nOur take: if AI caddie saves 1-2 strokes/round and you value those strokes, $99/year is reasonable." },
