       { h2: 'Club Suggestions — Virtual Caddie vs Nothing', body: "The Garmin S62 Virtual Caddie learns your actual distances over 5-10 rounds and suggests specific clubs for approach shots based on your data, wind, and elevation. In our testing, Virtual Caddie was right 68% of the time versus 52% for our own instincts.\n\nThe Apple Watch has no equivalent feature. Golfshot does not suggest clubs. Arccos on Apple Watch offers club suggestions, but that requires the full Arccos system ($179 + $99/year).\n\nThis is the single biggest differentiator. Virtual Caddie is included free with the S62 and genuinely improves club selection. Nothing on the Apple Watch ecosystem matches it without additional hardware and subscriptions.\n\nWinner: Garmin S62 — Virtual Caddie is free, effective, and unique." },
       { h2: 'Battery Life — The Dealbreaker', body: "Garmin S62: 20 hours GPS golf mode (4 rounds per charge). 12-14 days smartwatch mode.\n\nApple Watch: 6-8 hours with Golfshot running. 18-36 hours in normal use depending on model.\n\nThis is where the Apple Watch fundamentally fails as a golf device. A single 4.5-hour round with Golfshot drains 55-70% of the battery. If you play 36 holes, your Apple Watch dies mid-round. The Garmin handles 4 full rounds without charging.\n\nFor a device you wear daily, the Apple Watch needs nightly charging. The Garmin charges every 12-14 days. If you forget to charge the night before an early tee time, the Garmin still has battery. The Apple Watch is dead.\n\nWinner: Garmin S62 — not close. 20 hours vs 6-8 hours in golf mode." },
