     intro: `The best Trackman alternative in 2026 is the <strong>Bushnell Launch Pro</strong> at $2,499 — it uses the same Foresight GCQuad sensor technology that many tour fitters prefer, at one-seventh the price of a TrackMan 4. For budget-conscious golfers, the <strong>Garmin Approach R10</strong> ($599) provides 90 percent of the metrics that matter for practice at 3 percent of the cost.\n\nTrackman is the gold standard in launch monitors. Tour pros use it. Fitters use it. Teaching pros use it. But at $21,995+, it is priced for professionals, not weekend golfers. The good news: monitors costing 1/10th the price now deliver 90-95% of Trackman's accuracy. We tested seven alternatives to find the best one at each budget.`,
