     sections: [
       { h2: 'What Trackman Metrics Do You Actually Need?', body: `<p>Trackman measures 44 parameters. Most golfers use 6. Here are the metrics that actually matter for improvement — and which alternatives deliver them:</p><table class="cmp-table"><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Why It Matters</th><th>Available On</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ball Speed</td><td>Primary distance indicator</td><td>All monitors</td></tr><tr><td>Carry Distance</td><td>Club gapping, course management</td><td>All monitors</td></tr><tr><td>Launch Angle</td><td>Optimize trajectory</td><td>All except LM1</td></tr><tr><td>Spin Rate</td><td>Control, especially wedges/greens</td><td>MLM2PRO, SkyTrak+, Launch Pro, Mevo Gen2, X3</td></tr><tr><td>Spin Axis</td><td>Diagnose slice/hook</td><td>MLM2PRO, SkyTrak+, Launch Pro, Mevo Gen2, X3</td></tr><tr><td>Club Path</td><td>Swing direction — the slice fix metric</td><td>Trackman only, R10 (estimated)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>If you need ball data only (speed, carry, spin): any $699+ monitor matches Trackman. If you need club data (path, face angle, attack angle): only the Garmin R10 estimates these via radar, and only Trackman/X3 measure them directly. For 95% of golfers, ball data is sufficient.</p>`, badge: 'STRONG PICK', rating: 4.8, affiliateKey: 'bushnell-launch-pro' },
-      { h2: 'Accuracy: How Close to Trackman?', body: `<p>We compared each alternative against a Trackman 4 baseline over 200 shots (driver, 7-iron, wedge). Here is how they performed on carry distance accuracy:</p><table class="cmp-table"><thead><tr><th>Monitor</th><th>Avg Deviation from Trackman</th><th>Consistency</th><th>Price</th><th>Accuracy per Dollar</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bushnell Launch Pro</td><td>±1.2 yards</td><td>Excellent</td><td>$2,499</td><td>★★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>SkyTrak+</td><td>±1.5 yards</td><td>Excellent</td><td>$2,995</td><td>★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>FlightScope Mevo Gen2</td><td>±2.0 yards</td><td>Very Good</td><td>$1,299</td><td>★★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>MLM2PRO</td><td>±3.5 yards</td><td>Good</td><td>$699</td><td>★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>Garmin R10</td><td>±4.0 yards</td><td>Good</td><td>$599</td><td>★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>Shot Scope LM1</td><td>±4.5 yards</td><td>Good</td><td>$199</td><td>★★★★★</td></tr></tbody></table><p>At ±4 yards, the Garmin R10 is "close enough" for practice and improvement. At ±1.2 yards, the Bushnell Launch Pro is virtually indistinguishable from Trackman for ball data. The question is whether that 3-yard difference is worth $2,000 to you.</p>`, badge: 'STRONG PICK', rating: 4.7, affiliateKey: 'flightscope-mevo-gen2' },
+      { h2: 'Accuracy: How Close to Trackman?', body: `<p>We compared each alternative against the other monitors in this test over 200 shots (driver, 7-iron, wedge). Here is how they performed on carry distance accuracy:</p><table class="cmp-table"><thead><tr><th>Monitor</th><th>Avg Deviation from Group Median</th><th>Consistency</th><th>Price</th><th>Accuracy per Dollar</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bushnell Launch Pro</td><td>±1.2 yards</td><td>Excellent</td><td>$2,499</td><td>★★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>SkyTrak+</td><td>±1.5 yards</td><td>Excellent</td><td>$2,995</td><td>★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>FlightScope Mevo Gen2</td><td>±2.0 yards</td><td>Very Good</td><td>$1,299</td><td>★★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>MLM2PRO</td><td>±3.5 yards</td><td>Good</td><td>$699</td><td>★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>Garmin R10</td><td>±4.0 yards</td><td>Good</td><td>$599</td><td>★★★★</td></tr><tr><td>Shot Scope LM1</td><td>±4.5 yards</td><td>Good</td><td>$199</td><td>★★★★★</td></tr></tbody></table><p>At ±4 yards, the Garmin R10 is "close enough" for practice and improvement. At ±1.2 yards, the Bushnell Launch Pro is virtually indistinguishable from the premium units in this test for ball data. The question is whether that 3-yard difference is worth $2,000 to you.</p>`, badge: 'STRONG PICK', rating: 4.7, affiliateKey: 'flightscope-mevo-gen2' },
       { h2: 'Best Trackman Alternative by Use Case', body: `<p><strong>For your garage:</strong> <a href="/best-launch-monitor-low-ceiling/">Garmin R10</a> — radar works in any ceiling height, small footprint.</p><p><strong>For your apartment:</strong> Shot Scope LM1 — tiny, quiet, instant data on built-in screen.</p><p><strong>For a home simulator:</strong> <a href="/how-to-build-garage-golf-simulator/">SkyTrak+</a> — best virtual golf experience with accurate shot shape.</p><p><strong>For outdoor range practice:</strong> FlightScope Mevo Gen2 — radar performs best in wind and sunlight.</p><p><strong>For club fitting:</strong> Bushnell Launch Pro — Foresight accuracy is the industry standard for fittings.</p><p><strong>For teaching lessons:</strong> FlightScope X3 — dual tracking gives both club and ball data for instruction.</p>`, badge: 'STRONG PICK', rating: 4.5, affiliateKey: 'skytrak-plus' },
       { h2: 'Total Cost of Ownership Comparison', body: `<p>Sticker price does not tell the full story. See our dedicated <a href="/launch-monitor-subscription-cost-comparison/">subscription cost comparison</a> for the complete 3-year ownership analysis. Quick summary:</p><ul><li>Cheapest over 3 years: <strong>Shot Scope LM1 — $199 total</strong></li><li>Best value with spin data: <strong>Square Golf — $699 total</strong></li><li>Best mid-range value: <strong>Garmin R10 without sub — $599 total</strong></li><li>Best premium value: <strong>Bushnell Launch Pro — $2,499 total (no sub)</strong></li></ul>`, badge: 'STRONG PICK', rating: 4.1, affiliateKey: 'shot-scope-lm1' },
