-      { h2: 'Accuracy: How Close Are They?', body: '<p>We hit 200 shots with each monitor alongside a Trackman 4 baseline. The SkyTrak+ deviated ±1.5 yards from Trackman on carry distance. The MLM2PRO deviated ±3.5 yards. For context, that means on a 150-yard 7-iron, the SkyTrak+ reads 148.5-151.5 and the MLM2PRO reads 146.5-153.5.</p><p>Is ±2 yards worth $2,300? For most weekend golfers: no. Your natural shot dispersion is wider than 2 yards anyway. For club fitting or teaching: yes, every yard matters.</p>', badge: 'STRONG PICK', rating: 4.5, affiliateKey: 'skytrak-plus' },
