         <p style="margin:0 0 14px;">The accessories worth your money fall into two categories: cheap upgrades that improve your round disproportionately (a $25 putting mirror saves more strokes than a $400 driver), and expensive purchases that last long enough to justify the price (a quality push cart at $200 will serve you for 5+ seasons). The accessories that are not worth your money — most "swing tempo" gadgets, most weighted clubs, most putting alignment lasers — are flagged in our guides so you stop seeing them in your Amazon recommendations.</p>
